estion/problem "Given that $\\sqrt{3}-2\\text{i}=a+b\\text{i}$, calculate the value of $a$ and the value of $b.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we equate the real parts:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{3} & =a\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we equate the imaginary parts:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-2 & =b\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $a=\\sqrt{3}$ and $b=-2.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-70797/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1fe5d8aa-8a79-5de4-8566-1432a640d78f"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-70797"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-280585/field-1/219347bb4a6f51134d7f5aff5da33544f44afee934064621ebff9cf9e335ee59" :answer/id #uuid "a7988ca2-482d-5101-8787-45c6f2fa9f81" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-280585/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "5e6d2620-fe3a-575a-ba88-1d9684207c55" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-280585/field-1/219347bb4a6f51134d7f5aff5da33544f44afee934064621ebff9cf9e335ee59" :answer-field/choices ["q-280585/field-1/219347bb4a6f51134d7f5aff5da33544f44afee934064621ebff9cf9e335ee59"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-280585/field-2/a0e0e68f25b8b46aafef3b74aff7beff7fddc6de5bf36921680b04c7b0e6ffaa" :answer/id #uuid "450f2b2e-69c7-59ba-aacb-ca18991aa697" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-280585/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "0cbe6966-7990-54d8-a9ce-9a775583a065" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-280585/field-2/a0e0e68f25b8b46aafef3b74aff7beff7fddc6de5bf36921680b04c7b0e6ffaa" :answer-field/choices ["q-280585/field-2/a0e0e68f25b8b46aafef3b74aff7beff7fddc6de5bf36921680b04c7b0e6ffaa"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-280585" :question/id #uuid "77a56348-f84b-5d57-9641-9b5b6da0e05a" :question/math-academy-id "q-280585" :question/problem "If  $\\sqrt{5}+6\\text{i}=a+b\\text{i}$,  then$\\,a=$\n{{field-1}}\nand\n$b=$\n{{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "First, we equate the real parts:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{5} & =a\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we equate the imaginary parts:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6 & =b\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $a=\\sqrt{5}$ and $b=6.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-280585/field-1" "q-280585/field-2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1fe5d8aa-8a79-5de4-8566-1432a640d78f"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-280585"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-16552/selection/63aaf86ad8f5cd0b94ea5112446ed4553c83a266d1592a1fb0444b7e4a6dd274" :answer/id #uuid "02e5ebcf-50d7-5d71-9668-bcad2ca5ccf3" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$p=-3$, $q=2$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-16552/selection/b5efb3ad889aae4ff07c7c9245ec36b3a318d9ce80edaf9a72d141867aea648f" :answer/id #uuid "fcb8b0bd-5c8a-530e-99f7-ae9b14a3b6ca" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$p=\\frac{8}{3}$, $q=\\frac{1}{2}$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-16552/selection/42903519697fef4c582794e5020a7d68159ad11eddc5fb5628ba33d5136774f1" :answer/id #uuid "2fb50973-a875-53c7-b698-6e8764a19d60" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$p=-\\frac{3}{4}$, $q=\\frac{3}{2}$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-16552/selection/af50b98935decbc4fc252644a51428636402945a2ce7c002d12ba4e534fadfee" :answer/id #uuid "de98f9bd-100b-526c-96d1-fa7979cc37a7" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$p=\\frac{4}{3}$, $q=-\\frac{1}{2}$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-16552/selection/eaf94a17359c0258c707e198495aa3015e44751894fcd19b279bf75ac9b4e9e5" :answer/id #uuid "1f5561fe-a8ca-5906-a1ec-9766b8e26c10" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$p=-4$, $q=1$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-16552/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "a48499cc-b2a7-581d-a6cd-4e0b0ec06a8e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-16552/selection/b5efb3ad889aae4ff07c7c9245ec36b3a318d9ce80edaf9a72d141867aea648f" :answer-field/choices ["q-16552/selection/63aaf86ad8f5cd0b94ea5112446ed4553c83a266d1592a1fb0444b7e4a6dd274" "q-16552/selection/b5efb3ad889aae4ff07c7c9245ec36b3a318d9ce80edaf9a72d141867aea648f" "q-16552/selection/42903519697fef4c582794e5020a7d68159ad11eddc5fb5628ba33d5136774f1" "q-16552/selection/af50b98935decbc4fc252644a51428636402945a2ce7c002d12ba4e534fadfee" "q-16552/selection/eaf94a17359c0258c707e198495aa3015e44751894fcd19b279bf75ac9b4e9e5"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-16552" :question/id #uuid "9dabd258-08a3-5975-8674-6e9f1bd600ca" :question/math-academy-id "q-16552" :question/problem "Given that $\\frac{3p+2q\\text{i}}{2-3\\text{i}}=1+2\\text{i}$, calculate $p$ and $q.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we multiply both sides of the equation by $2-3\\text{i}$ to get rid of the fraction and isolate the variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3p+2q\\text{i}}{2-3\\text{i}} & =1+2\\text{i} \\\\ 3p+2q\\text{i} & =(1+2\\text{i})(2-3\\text{i}) \\\\ 3p+2q\\text{i} & =2-3\\text{i}+4\\text{i}-6{\\text{i}}^{2} \\\\ 3p+2q\\text{i} & =2+\\text{i}-6(-1) \\\\ 3p+2q\\text{i} & =8+\\text{i}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can equate the real parts and the imaginary parts separately.\n\n- Equating the real parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3p & =8 \\\\ p & =\\frac{8}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Equating the imaginary parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2q & =1 \\\\ q & =\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $p=\\frac{8}{3}$ and $q=\\frac{1}{2}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-16552/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1bbe2fe7-b69c-54f3-9f1c-3369e3f1395d"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-16552"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-275089/field-1/66dedd51c696580d351ab6a45c1c63cb495081ccf219c3c3c62f1d90fbeb5a49" :answer/id #uuid "91d4dccc-27c6-51a4-b54f-1bc0468fd8f9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "15" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-275089/field-1/0f0db3a18f1d79c4863315eefe754cc5306e04e7aeebf4414ffedb95d6f1bc97" :answer/id #uuid "eb8909ea-3d4a-5901-98ff-99851ac32a34" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "12" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-275089/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "ed68bc47-c290-5df5-bb0f-473aa53e7443" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-275089/field-1/66dedd51c696580d351ab6a45c1c63cb495081ccf219c3c3c62f1d90fbeb5a49" :answer-field/choices ["q-275089/field-1/66dedd51c696580d351ab6a45c1c63cb495081ccf219c3c3c62f1d90fbeb5a49" "q-275089/field-1/0f0db3a18f1d79c4863315eefe754cc5306e04e7aeebf4414ffedb95d6f1bc97"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-275089/field-2/650efaaa01beaa7de6c030497edff1dd29c570bf683f3726bbcacabc3dfa7e4c" :answer/id #uuid "dbcf42e3-62bb-53a9-b3cf-d54527113087" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "16" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-275089/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "c78e8003-b7ca-58de-a2db-f7d083140417" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-275089/field-2/650efaaa01beaa7de6c030497edff1dd29c570bf683f3726bbcacabc3dfa7e4c" :answer-field/choices ["q-275089/field-2/650efaaa01beaa7de6c030497edff1dd29c570bf683f3726bbcacabc3dfa7e4c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-275089" :question/id #uuid "c49dd4d9-a6cd-5226-8787-0dd1f2c141a5" :question/math-academy-id "q-275089" :question/problem "If  $6-\\text{i}=\\frac{p+q\\text{i}}{2+3\\text{i}},$ then$\\,p=$\n{{field-1}}\nand\n$q=$\n{{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "First, we multiply both sides of the equation by $2+3\\text{i}$ to get rid of the fraction and isolate the variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6-\\text{i}=\\frac{p+q\\text{i}}{2+3\\text{i}} \\\\ (6-\\text{i})(2+3\\text{i}) & =p+q\\text{i} \\\\ 12+18\\text{i}-2\\text{i}-3{\\text{i}}^{2} & =p+q\\text{i} \\\\ 12+3+16\\text{i} & =p+q\\text{i} \\\\ 15+16\\text{i} & =p+q\\text{i}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can equate the real parts and the imaginary parts separately.\n\n- Equating the real parts, we get\n\n$$\n15=p.\n$$\n\n- Equating the imaginary parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}16 & =q.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $p=15$ and $q=16.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-275089/field-1" "q-275089/field-2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1bbe2fe7-b69c-54f3-9f1c-3369e3f1395d"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-275089"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-8412/selection/73c721cdef6d95efe7b8aa3b197697ba5a6c390bddb07b83b7ac019889694d4f" :answer/id #uuid "c95d874b-a082-5c74-b132-481dcbda63be" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$p=\\frac{2}{5}$, $q=\\frac{4}{5}$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-8412/selection/e08d3165fdc3fb7e170e6cba53507385524a608bd0ad90827dc3abdb71565532" :answer/id #uuid "75de96a6-1dee-5fb7-b4dd-6f59a69acba3" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$p=1$, $q=-\\,\\frac{3}{5}$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-8412/selection/048f9a04435e60fd5f3a4db3606e9eef8766e9037019e065699407d0c346e7d8" :answer/id #uuid "4a545094-50fd-5a76-909c-15cbb359a2a4" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$p=-4$, $q=-3$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-8412/selection/b4052fc36f1306ec34bb873f63630982097c3cf4a9d6c476e8e016035d7a7dbc" :answer/id #uuid "5b1e9a44-349c-554e-aece-cab5090e5be3" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$p=\\frac{1}{5}$, $q=-\\,\\frac{3}{5}$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-8412/selection/95c2f6ef953411f82c8e4d875da18999745f9f44e11c42c87b913d20a1e85593" :answer/id #uuid "95a5a1f0-6169-5838-a450-3087c4f7d450" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$p=5$, $q=4$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-8412/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "e45da950-da9c-5489-bd7a-dc764d54a054" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-8412/selection/95c2f6ef953411f82c8e4d875da18999745f9f44e11c42c87b913d20a1e85593" :answer-field/choices ["q-8412/selection/73c721cdef6d95efe7b8aa3b197697ba5a6c390bddb07b83b7ac019889694d4f" "q-8412/selection/e08d3165fdc3fb7e170e6cba53507385524a608bd0ad90827dc3abdb71565532" "q-8412/selection/048f9a04435e60fd5f3a4db3606e9eef8766e9037019e065699407d0c346e7d8" "q-8412/selection/b4052fc36f1306ec34bb873f63630982097c3cf4a9d6c476e8e016035d7a7dbc" "q-8412/selection/95c2f6ef953411f82c8e4d875da18999745f9f44e11c42c87b913d20a1e85593"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-8412" :question/id #uuid "196e7c79-56bb-55f4-85a9-98019ba4d55e" :question/math-academy-id "q-8412" :question/problem "Given that $\\frac{6+13\\text{i}}{5}=\\frac{p+\\text{i}q}{2-\\text{i}}$, calculate $p$ and $q.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we multiply both sides of the equation by $2-\\text{i}$ to get rid of the fraction and isolate the variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{6+13\\text{i}}{5} & =\\frac{p+\\text{i}q}{2-\\text{i}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{5}(6+13\\text{i})(2-\\text{i}) & =p+\\text{i}q \\\\ \\frac{1}{5}(12-6\\text{i}+26\\text{i}-13{\\text{i}}^{2}) & =p+\\text{i}q \\\\ \\frac{1}{5}(12+13+20\\text{i}) & =p+\\text{i}q \\\\ \\frac{1}{5}(25+20\\text{i}) & =p+\\text{i}q \\\\ 5+4\\text{i} & =p+\\text{i}q\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can equate the real parts and the imaginary parts separately.\n\n- Equating the real parts, we get\n\n$$\n5=p.\n$$\n\n- Equating the imaginary parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4 & =q.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $p=5$ and $q=4.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-8412/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1bbe2fe7-b69c-54f3-9f1c-3369e3f1395d"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-8412"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-8408/selection/e2414c0eedc98b5ddf0526a5a5461d85c31868762acd5a918929adede443679b" :answer/id #uuid "f831ecd3-fa88-52c4-b269-76da2f26bc5e" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$p=-6$, $q=-4$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-8408/selection/ac77b90d982717a466fd3673d0e6b4c5c21c47b766409480ad16aa3e59d434b8" :answer/id #uuid "ad201510-e91e-5a79-a59b-fe01d0db7a1f" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$p=6$, $q=-4$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-8408/selection/66620fa72116de6a1c7ab974b1747da9d5a3faa176b3e70f5dbff40b02f28c46" :answer/id #uuid "4f72c1c1-4681-52d3-9806-924ac41c942b" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$p=-4$, $q=-6$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-8408/selection/46c42ada6abcb41716851769cb8fc1f8b3012e31f1b8a5641539378cd1189aeb" :answer/id #uuid "67081898-0835-5e62-8403-84093bb80e0b" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$p=4$, $q=-6$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-8408/selection/68c547c61926f6e7e2c2fb2bf91ef4aa27f3f24962288287be282e2eac931ef4" :answer/id #uuid "d3c6a741-93f1-55c8-bea5-52582c7c35ac" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$p=2$, $q=-3$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-8408/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "fba79f83-12a3-5026-a958-4a08db991d3a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-8408/selection/46c42ada6abcb41716851769cb8fc1f8b3012e31f1b8a5641539378cd1189aeb" :answer-field/choices ["q-8408/selection/e2414c0eedc98b5ddf0526a5a5461d85c31868762acd5a918929adede443679b" "q-8408/selection/ac77b90d982717a466fd3673d0e6b4c5c21c47b766409480ad16aa3e59d434b8" "q-8408/selection/66620fa72116de6a1c7ab974b1747da9d5a3faa176b3e70f5dbff40b02f28c46" "q-8408/selection/46c42ada6abcb41716851769cb8fc1f8b3012e31f1b8a5641539378cd1189aeb" "q-8408/selection/68c547c61926f6e7e2c2fb2bf91ef4aa27f3f24962288287be282e2eac931ef4"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-8408" :question/id #uuid "216ae57a-81ed-5f5e-b145-ffbb67f1cde3" :question/math-academy-id "q-8408" :question/problem "Given that $-3-2\\text{i}=\\frac{p+\\text{i}q}{2\\text{i}}$, calculate $p$ and $q.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we multiply both sides of the equation by $2\\text{i}$ to get rid of the fraction and isolate the variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-3-2\\text{i} & =\\frac{p+\\text{i}q}{2\\text{i}} \\\\ 2\\text{i}(-3-2\\text{i}) & =p+\\text{i}q \\\\ -6\\text{i}-4{\\text{i}}^{2} & =p+\\text{i}q \\\\ 4-6\\text{i} & =p+\\text{i}q\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can equate the real parts and the imaginary parts separately.\n\n- Equating the real parts, we get\n\n$$\n4=p.\n$$\n\n- Equating the imaginary parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-6 & =q.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $p=4$ and $q=-6.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-8408/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1bbe2fe7-b69c-54f3-9f1c-3369e3f1395d"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-8408"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-160043/selection/74493570d8a0bf599db6168c52a62b20b80ee56358113b92407adfc011c15508" :answer/id #uuid "92fa84e7-8288-5fe8-88e2-2c3b2c32e2c9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "p=-2,q=3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-160043/selection/91f9361ccb6c082135f70ca5fa58bba56d99528808e3c3f10ba0a93eb059605d" :answer/id #uuid "5d50f5ac-1165-5b25-8272-dbd5d92ba7ad" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "p=-1,q=4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-160043/selection/beec6eafb26243dcaae39f66a5f23bc172464c807670040ea323e3f983abc8db" :answer/id #uuid "03ca134f-54ff-51be-9740-1b6a99a86ec2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "p=-1,q=-4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-160043/selection/59a1dc4b7178609368aed29ac0b3f9d89fe30372490df7ca6a534210dab79375" :answer/id #uuid "46bbb13c-ab62-57bc-9023-58dd905ed711" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "p=-2,q=-8" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-160043/selection/d4500d4fc2f4218b4f3434b3e3fcc17d83b2746509150bbec6fb9ccd45cba8c3" :answer/id #uuid "4807703d-ea87-5aad-a030-79582c32c7dd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "p=-4,q=2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-160043/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "f67d1dfe-3a13-519d-8ab9-ea6af168825e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-160043/selection/59a1dc4b7178609368aed29ac0b3f9d89fe30372490df7ca6a534210dab79375" :answer-field/choices ["q-160043/selection/74493570d8a0bf599db6168c52a62b20b80ee56358113b92407adfc011c15508" "q-160043/selection/91f9361ccb6c082135f70ca5fa58bba56d99528808e3c3f10ba0a93eb059605d" "q-160043/selection/beec6eafb26243dcaae39f66a5f23bc172464c807670040ea323e3f983abc8db" "q-160043/selection/59a1dc4b7178609368aed29ac0b3f9d89fe30372490df7ca6a534210dab79375" "q-160043/selection/d4500d4fc2f4218b4f3434b3e3fcc17d83b2746509150bbec6fb9ccd45cba8c3"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-160043" :question/id #uuid "1273a17f-9601-5e3d-93d7-d4842c398726" :question/math-academy-id "q-160043" :question/problem "Given that $-4+\\text{i}=\\frac{p+\\text{i}q}{2\\text{i}},$ calculate $p$ and $q.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we multiply both sides of the equation by $2\\text{i}$ to get rid of the fraction and isolate the variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-4+\\text{i} & =\\frac{p+\\text{i}q}{2\\text{i}} \\\\ (-4+\\text{i})(2\\text{i}) & =p+\\text{i}q \\\\ -8\\text{i}+2{\\text{i}}^{2} & =p+\\text{i}q \\\\ -2-8\\text{i} & =p+\\text{i}q\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can equate the real parts and the imaginary parts separately.\n\n- Equating the real parts, we get\n\n$$\n-2=p.\n$$\n\n- Equating the imaginary parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-8 & =q.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $p=-2$ and $q=-8.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-160043/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1bbe2fe7-b69c-54f3-9f1c-3369e3f1395d"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-160043"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-8036"] :question/problem "Given that $5-\\text{i}=(p+\\text{i}q)(3+2\\text{i})$, calculate $p$ and $q.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we divide both sides of the equation by $3+2\\text{i}$ to isolate the variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5-\\text{i} & =(p+\\text{i}q)(3+2\\text{i}) \\\\ \\frac{5-\\text{i}}{3+2\\text{i}} & =p+\\text{i}q\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to simplify the fraction on the left-hand side, we multiply the numerator and denominator by the conjugate of the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(5-\\text{i})(3-2\\text{i})}{(3+2\\text{i})(3-2\\text{i})} & =p+\\text{i}q \\\\ \\frac{15-3\\text{i}-10\\text{i}+2{\\text{i}}^{2}}{{3}^{2}-(2\\text{i})^{2}} & =p+\\text{i}q \\\\ \\frac{13-13\\text{i}}{9+4} & =p+\\text{i}q \\\\ \\frac{13-13\\text{i}}{13} & =p+\\text{i}q \\\\ 1-\\text{i} & =p+\\text{i}q\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can equate the real parts and the imaginary parts separately.\n\n- Equating the real parts, we get $1=p.$\n\n- Equating the imaginary parts, we get $-1=q.$\n\nTherefore, $p=1$ and $q=-1.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-160049/selection/800fac99616253aeb3ff6ae82700d99474db25801fc7a4112f7568ff5dad9b48" :answer/id #uuid "f1d591eb-6b58-5f15-9e36-44f9420dc798" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "p=\\frac{3}{5},q=-\\frac{3}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-160049/selection/2c633cec53030bfc8b323bc6924f204c921936dd56226385cbeeb1c21145b704" :answer/id #uuid "45c8b7f2-9be5-55b5-a22b-e054f4cbe1af" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "p=-\\frac{3}{2},q=\\frac{3}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-160049/selection/537050a2e7505c454d57ab54ab720f0f4eede66f4811b8254e26ee788adbdd4c" :answer/id #uuid "ba57b036-ebae-511e-91ae-a387bf1362b8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "p=\\frac{3}{2},q=-\\frac{3}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-160049/selection/8ad1bc909430477637861a94ae07d988e46a1f2685824b300b3a7ab3ce74c2b1" :answer/id #uuid "8c53c1c6-f880-529f-9ea9-1db90afcb2e6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "p=\\frac{2}{5},q=-\\frac{1}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-160049/selection/b695a8d3f863f2d15a2cedc2a41fa83d3c335a1a1d66b6a1edb5dd71738a9216" :answer/id #uuid "c4270e82-24f8-5ea2-8d59-88b154a06aeb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "p=\\frac{3}{2},q=-\\frac{1}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-160049/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "37604755-f009-5aae-942f-1a1f1e4a3997" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-160049/selection/b695a8d3f863f2d15a2cedc2a41fa83d3c335a1a1d66b6a1edb5dd71738a9216" :answer-field/choices ["q-160049/selection/800fac99616253aeb3ff6ae82700d99474db25801fc7a4112f7568ff5dad9b48" "q-160049/selection/2c633cec53030bfc8b323bc6924f204c921936dd56226385cbeeb1c21145b704" "q-160049/selection/537050a2e7505c454d57ab54ab720f0f4eede66f4811b8254e26ee788adbdd4c" "q-160049/selection/8ad1bc909430477637861a94ae07d988e46a1f2685824b300b3a7ab3ce74c2b1" "q-160049/selection/b695a8d3f863f2d15a2cedc2a41fa83d3c335a1a1d66b6a1edb5dd71738a9216"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-160049" :question/id #uuid "050685d3-106a-556e-94cf-f2ab6b33d435" :question/math-academy-id "q-160049" :question/problem "Given that $5=(p+q\\text{i})(3+\\text{i})$, calculate $p$ and $q.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we divide both sides of the equation by $3+\\text{i}$ to isolate the variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5 & =(p+q\\text{i})(3+\\text{i}) \\\\ \\frac{5}{3+\\text{i}} & =p+q\\text{i}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to simplify the fraction on the left-hand side, we multiply the numerator and denominator by the conjugate of the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(5)(3-\\text{i})}{(3+\\text{i})(3-\\text{i})} & =p+q\\text{i} \\\\ \\frac{15-5\\text{i}}{{3}^{2}-(\\text{i})^{2}} & =p+q\\text{i} \\\\ \\frac{15-5\\text{i}}{9+1} & =p+q\\text{i} \\\\ \\frac{15-5\\text{i}}{10} & =p+q\\text{i} \\\\ \\frac{3}{2}-\\frac{1}{2}\\text{i} & =p+q\\text{i}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can equate the real parts and the imaginary parts separately.\n\n- Equating the real parts, we get $\\frac{3}{2}=p.$\n\n- Equating the imaginary parts, we get $-\\frac{1}{2}=q.$\n\nTherefore, $p=\\frac{3}{2}$ and $q=-\\frac{1}{2}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-160049/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c9f40a0e-83f3-5814-b9a1-8b1265fe93cc"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-160049"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} [:db/retract 17592186060351 :question/answer-fields 17592186059089] {:db/id "q-8407/selection/ma-v1/69a971dd4fb3a91964354d7735d9bc65c3d020b0ae5f5af57310ce9ceacaae76/9769b7ba6947e40e8d51f600c644176a1f0c5ac09bc718458bd09f8311df4ba2" :answer/id #uuid "ed6ecd6c-28ca-5546-b66f-890e2dfb2a02" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$p=-1$, $q=1$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-8407/selection/ma-v1/69a971dd4fb3a91964354d7735d9bc65c3d020b0ae5f5af57310ce9ceacaae76/2b970d25b917835b4824eb9d85564f0c0e32049ebb5f83c9af07657a47b38acb" :answer/id #uuid "917c4db6-b341-58ff-ba46-14f05344deae" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$p=2$, $q=3$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-8407/selection/ma-v1/69a971dd4fb3a91964354d7735d9bc65c3d020b0ae5f5af57310ce9ceacaae76/291e842906d43741ecdf5be248020819eddaa542d3dbe877ce311f55719423e3" :answer/id #uuid "f741c71e-befa-5d0f-b026-df1cd168e239" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$p=3$, $q=-4$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-8407/selection/ma-v1/69a971dd4fb3a91964354d7735d9bc65c3d020b0ae5f5af57310ce9ceacaae76/4d09a00751e0c0721350f0fe3c0e70dfeb5f2fe40e644c768b1bd6f27316fe0e" :answer/id #uuid "ea59a192-9ad0-57e4-918d-3e77cac380ee" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$p=-5$, $q=2$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-8407/selection/ma-v1/69a971dd4fb3a91964354d7735d9bc65c3d020b0ae5f5af57310ce9ceacaae76/63aaf86ad8f5cd0b94ea5112446ed4553c83a266d1592a1fb0444b7e4a6dd274" :answer/id #uuid "f972a3be-8786-59f6-bf96-15c2afdd48c9" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$p=-3$, $q=2$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-8407/selection/ma-v1/69a971dd4fb3a91964354d7735d9bc65c3d020b0ae5f5af57310ce9ceacaae76" :answer-field/id #uuid "7134303b-3280-56f4-98af-02b5c1ea53ad" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-8407/selection/ma-v1/69a971dd4fb3a91964354d7735d9bc65c3d020b0ae5f5af57310ce9ceacaae76/63aaf86ad8f5cd0b94ea5112446ed4553c83a266d1592a1fb0444b7e4a6dd274" :answer-field/choices ["q-8407/selection/ma-v1/69a971dd4fb3a91964354d7735d9bc65c3d020b0ae5f5af57310ce9ceacaae76/9769b7ba6947e40e8d51f600c644176a1f0c5ac09bc718458bd09f8311df4ba2" "q-8407/selection/ma-v1/69a971dd4fb3a91964354d7735d9bc65c3d020b0ae5f5af57310ce9ceacaae76/2b970d25b917835b4824eb9d85564f0c0e32049ebb5f83c9af07657a47b38acb" "q-8407/selection/ma-v1/69a971dd4fb3a91964354d7735d9bc65c3d020b0ae5f5af57310ce9ceacaae76/291e842906d43741ecdf5be248020819eddaa542d3dbe877ce311f55719423e3" "q-8407/selection/ma-v1/69a971dd4fb3a91964354d7735d9bc65c3d020b0ae5f5af57310ce9ceacaae76/4d09a00751e0c0721350f0fe3c0e70dfeb5f2fe40e644c768b1bd6f27316fe0e" "q-8407/selection/ma-v1/69a971dd4fb3a91964354d7735d9bc65c3d020b0ae5f5af57310ce9ceacaae76/63aaf86ad8f5cd0b94ea5112446ed4553c83a266d1592a1fb0444b7e4a6dd274"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-8407"] :question/problem "Given that $\\frac{13\\text{i}}{2-3\\text{i}}=p+\\text{i}q,$ calculate $p$ and $q.$" :question/worked-solution "First, to simplify the fraction on the left-hand side, we multiply the numerator and denominator by the conjugate of the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{13\\text{i}(2+3\\text{i})}{(2-3\\text{i})(2+3\\text{i})} & =p+\\text{i}q \\\\ \\frac{13\\text{i}(2+3\\text{i})}{(2)^{2}-(3\\text{i})^{2}} & =p+\\text{i}q \\\\ \\frac{13\\text{i}(2+3\\text{i})}{13} & =p+\\text{i}q \\\\ \\text{i}(2+3\\text{i}) & =p+\\text{i}q \\\\ 2\\text{i}+3{\\text{i}}^{2} & =p+\\text{i}q \\\\ -3+2\\text{i} & =p+\\text{i}q\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can equate the real parts and the imaginary parts separately.\n\n- Equating the real parts, we get $-3=p.$\n\n- Equating the imaginary parts, we get $2=q.$\n\nTherefore, $p=-3$ and $q=2.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-8407/selection/ma-v1/69a971dd4fb3a91964354d7735d9bc65c3d020b0ae5f5af57310ce9ceacaae76"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-280406/field-1/67dca9eae8121d587dbf3a6645e4651b4f4ad5581f802a1da93ef77ae21c14bd" :answer/id #uuid "c0718f95-8035-5523-be2a-734012216cab" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{16}{13}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-280406/field-1/58fbd1f6e87f8f49fef88f07b9e94941a8c833749626d724ec2dad2befaf0a80" :answer/id #uuid "39a9c4f1-d473-518a-a950-2f61222073fe" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{32}{13}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-280406/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "80a7f906-2981-596b-9a0a-6538b3776ea3" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-280406/field-1/67dca9eae8121d587dbf3a6645e4651b4f4ad5581f802a1da93ef77ae21c14bd" :answer-field/choices ["q-280406/field-1/67dca9eae8121d587dbf3a6645e4651b4f4ad5581f802a1da93ef77ae21c14bd" "q-280406/field-1/58fbd1f6e87f8f49fef88f07b9e94941a8c833749626d724ec2dad2befaf0a80"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-280406/field-2/976f0114964c1ac01a3961d2740c4467a509c8684ddf07694051af1c668e2e47" :answer/id #uuid "5198a42b-e7f3-5abb-9d87-3f5adab37bcc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{9}{65}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-280406/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "4056c54e-298f-5c3e-a5ee-89c1961d9f79" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-280406/field-2/976f0114964c1ac01a3961d2740c4467a509c8684ddf07694051af1c668e2e47" :answer-field/choices ["q-280406/field-2/976f0114964c1ac01a3961d2740c4467a509c8684ddf07694051af1c668e2e47"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-280406" :question/id #uuid "6b34ee7b-9dc7-52b2-9d59-2025071a0239" :question/math-academy-id "q-280406" :question/problem "Given that $\\frac{6-7\\text{i}}{3-2\\text{i}}=2p-5q\\text{i}$, then$\\,p=$\n{{field-1}}\nand\n$q=$\n{{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "First, to simplify the fraction on the left-hand side, we multiply the numerator and denominator by the conjugate of the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{6-7\\text{i}}{3-2\\text{i}} & =2p-5q\\text{i} \\\\ \\frac{(6-7\\text{i})(3+2\\text{i})}{(3-2\\text{i})(3+2\\text{i})} & =2p-5q\\text{i} \\\\ \\frac{18+12\\text{i}-21\\text{i}-14{\\text{i}}^{2}}{{3}^{2}+{2}^{2}} & =2p-5q\\text{i} \\\\ \\frac{18-9\\text{i}-14(-1)}{13} & =2p-5q\\text{i} \\\\ \\frac{32-9\\text{i}}{13} & =2p-5q\\text{i} \\\\ \\frac{32}{13}-\\frac{9}{13}\\text{i} & =2p-5q\\text{i}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can equate the real parts and the imaginary parts separately.\n\n- Equating the real parts, we get $\\frac{32}{13}=2p.$\n\n- Equating the imaginary parts, we get $-\\frac{9}{13}=-5q.$\n\nTherefore, $p=\\frac{16}{13}$ and $q=\\frac{9}{65}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-280406/field-1" "q-280406/field-2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c9f40a0e-83f3-5814-b9a1-8b1265fe93cc"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-280406"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-160050/selection/4bfe3460fc3113d4d2452a838be06630679a0c6213292accd8dcbf69cb37a66b" :answer/id #uuid "8a1d09b0-d145-5d5e-9776-9d4f5468cd5b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "p=-2,q=1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-160050/selection/09bc56451d219e94a3e89aa8d022546a51462decf45153ef457f2165256da0e1" :answer/id #uuid "e7a7c332-9fb8-5488-b6aa-7afa28cd75c4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "p=-1,q=1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-160050/selection/3e0f18fbeaa65c084d89db01713760557ddaad3bdb2639f45d83f8cf33dd55f9" :answer/id #uuid "51f1a684-8ad3-553d-9551-edb51a5e4097" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "p=1,q=1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-160050/selection/af7a5a87f55296d326830728289a8424e92b9f6db40ef3eb8e4ea4b1c52477f1" :answer/id #uuid "6070670a-3387-5464-9508-e4edb16634d8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "p=-1,q=2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-160050/selection/3fe6eee520109ecc4b148128d4c7942b14733ee366062b0b86d4517db2f4adf3" :answer/id #uuid "c7f28ec3-5678-5756-ac7e-708b04a20a9e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "p=2,q=1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-160050/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "97a5ea3f-9e83-58d6-9b5b-e34e8edd2ed5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-160050/selection/09bc56451d219e94a3e89aa8d022546a51462decf45153ef457f2165256da0e1" :answer-field/choices ["q-160050/selection/4bfe3460fc3113d4d2452a838be06630679a0c6213292accd8dcbf69cb37a66b" "q-160050/selection/09bc56451d219e94a3e89aa8d022546a51462decf45153ef457f2165256da0e1" "q-160050/selection/3e0f18fbeaa65c084d89db01713760557ddaad3bdb2639f45d83f8cf33dd55f9" "q-160050/selection/af7a5a87f55296d326830728289a8424e92b9f6db40ef3eb8e4ea4b1c52477f1" "q-160050/selection/3fe6eee520109ecc4b148128d4c7942b14733ee366062b0b86d4517db2f4adf3"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-160050" :question/id #uuid "77d9662b-7262-5332-935d-549a31e7f0a1" :question/math-academy-id "q-160050" :question/problem "Given that $1+7\\text{i}=(p+\\text{i}q)(3-4\\text{i})$, calculate $p$ and $q.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we divide both sides of the equation by $3-4\\text{i}$ to isolate the\n  variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1+7\\text{i} & =(p+\\text{i}q)(3-4\\text{i}) \\\\ \\frac{1+7\\text{i}}{3-4\\text{i}} & =p+\\text{i}q\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to simplify the fraction on the left-hand side, we multiply the numerator and denominator by the conjugate of the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(1+7\\text{i})(3+4\\text{i})}{(3-4\\text{i})(3+4\\text{i})} & =p+\\text{i}q \\\\ \\frac{3+21\\text{i}+4\\text{i}+28{\\text{i}}^{2}}{{3}^{2}-(4\\text{i})^{2}} & =p+\\text{i}q \\\\ \\frac{-25+25\\text{i}}{9+16} & =p+\\text{i}q \\\\ \\frac{-25+25\\text{i}}{25} & =p+\\text{i}q \\\\ -1+\\text{i} & =p+\\text{i}q\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can equate the real parts and the imaginary parts separately.\n\n- Equating the real parts, we get $-1=p.$\n\n- Equating the imaginary parts, we get $1=q.$\n\nTherefore, $p=-1$ and $q=1.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-160050/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c9f40a0e-83f3-5814-b9a1-8b1265fe93cc"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-160050"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-5245"] :question/problem "Given that $3+2\\textrm{i} = a + \\textrm{i}b,$ calculate the value of $a$ and the value of $b.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we equate the real parts:\n\n$$\n3 = a\n$$\n\nThen, we equate the imaginary parts:\n\n$$\n2 = b\n$$\n\nTherefore, $a=3$ and $b=2.$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-5261"] :question/problem "Given that $2 - 3 \\textrm{i} = \\dfrac{p - 2q \\textrm{i} }{1 + 2 \\textrm{i}},$ calculate $p$ and $q.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we multiply both sides of the equation by $1+2\\textrm{i}$ to get rid of the fraction and isolate the variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2-3\\text{i} & =\\frac{p-2q\\text{i}}{1+2\\text{i}} \\\\ (2-3\\text{i})(1+2\\text{i}) & =p-2q\\text{i} \\\\ 2+4\\text{i}-3\\text{i}-6{\\text{i}}^{2} & =p-2q\\text{i} \\\\ 2+\\text{i}-6(-1) & =p-2q\\text{i} \\\\ 8+\\text{i} & =p-2q\\text{i}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can equate the real parts and the imaginary parts separately.\n\n- Equating the real parts, we get\n\n$$\n8 = p.\n$$\n\n- Equating the imaginary parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1 & =-2q \\\\ q & =-\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $p=8$ and $q = -\\dfrac{1}{2}.$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-5293"] :question/problem "Given that $3+5\\textrm{i} = (p+\\textrm{i}q)(1+\\textrm{i}),$ calculate $p$ and $q.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we divide both sides of the equation by $1+\\textrm{i}$ to isolate the variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3+5\\text{i} & =(p+\\text{i}q)(1+\\text{i}) \\\\ \\frac{3+5\\text{i}}{1+\\text{i}} & =p+\\text{i}q\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to simplify the fraction on the left-hand side, we multiply the numerator and denominator by the conjugate of the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(3+5\\text{i})(1-\\text{i})}{(1+\\text{i})(1-\\text{i})} & =p+\\text{i}q \\\\ \\frac{3-3\\text{i}+5\\text{i}-5{\\text{i}}^{2}}{{1}^{2}-{\\text{i}}^{2}} & =p+\\text{i}q \\\\ \\frac{3+2\\text{i}-5(-1)}{1-(-1)} & =p+\\text{i}q \\\\ \\frac{8+2\\text{i}}{2} & =p+\\text{i}q \\\\ 4+\\text{i} & =p+\\text{i}q\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can equate the real parts and the imaginary parts separately.\n\n- Equating the real parts, we get $4=p.$\n\n- Equating the imaginary parts, we get $1=q.$\n\nTherefore, $p=4$ and $q=1.$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]}]
